              * gdprConsentRequired and vendor.consent on this cookie at submit time
              * (UtilityManager::eloquaVendorConsentGiven), so the cookie must always carry
              * Didomi's current determination rather than the fail-closed defaults that
              * ukg_cookies.js writes on first visit.
              *
              * Deliberately ungated. Any "has the visitor chosen yet" predicate — a
              * created/updated timestamp gap, or Didomi.shouldConsentBeCollected() — skips
              * exactly the visitors whose cookie is still holding those defaults. Reducing
              * redundant writes is the job of the change detection inside
              * updateU20K20GCookieWithGdprProperties(), not of a gate out here.
